  "tour": "2026 Summer Tour",
  "notes": "<p>This show was Phish's 96th performance at Madison Square Garden and featured songs from 1996 as well as multiple references to <a href=\"https://phish.net/faq/clifford-ball\">The Clifford Ball</a>: Trey and Mike wore their iconic outfits, and <span>The Harpua narration freed Jimmy from his </span><a href=\"https://phish.net/setlists/phish-august-17-1996-plattsburgh-air-force-base-plattsburgh-ny-usa\"><span>30 year prison of vibration above Plattsburgh, NY</span></a><span>.</span> Before the show, the light rig approximated the NY Knicks' logo. This show featured multiple bustouts: The Star Spangled Banner <span>(last played </span><a href=\"https://phish.net/setlists/phish-december-28-2016-madison-square-garden-new-york-ny-usa.html\"><span>December 28, 2016</span></a><span>, or 362 shows), Talk (last played </span><a href=\"https://phish.net/setlists/phish-october-13-2023-united-center-chicago-il-usa.html\"><span>October 13, 2023</span></a><span>, or 122 shows), Harpua (last played </span><a href=\"https://phish.net/setlists/phish-december-31-2023-madison-square-garden-new-york-ny-usa.html\"><span>December 31, 2023</span></a><span>, or 116 shows), and Suspicious Minds (last played </span><a href=\"https://phish.net/setlists/phish-december-06-1996-the-aladdin-theatre-las-vegas-nv-usa.html\"><span>December 6, 1996</span></a><span>, or 1021 shows). In Axilla (Part II) Trey began the lyrics to part I, said \"Wait </span><a href=\"https://phish.net/setlists/phish-july-22-2026-madison-square-garden-new-york-ny-usa\"><span>we did that one already</span></a><span>\", and sang part II. In YEM, Trey played the mini drum kit. In I Didn't Know Trey introduced Fish as Elvis Presley; Fish performed multiple Elvis antics. Fish teased Buffalo Bill in Crosseyed and Painless.</span></p>",
  "permalink": "https://phish.net/setlists/phish-july-29-2026-madison-square-garden-new-york-ny-usa.html",
